<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Knäred</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1613">1613</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Knäred · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-war">Kalmar War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Knäred, signed on 20 January 1613, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-war">Kalmar War</a> between Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Sweden gave up its claims in the far north of Norway and agreed to pay a ransom of one million riksdaler for the return of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvsborg">Älvsborg</a>, its only port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>, which Christian IV had taken.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-knared.jpg" alt="Treaty of Knäred" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rickard Törnblad · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_Kn%C3%A4red_Memorial_Stone,_Sj%C3%B6ared,_Halland,_Sweden_(1)_-_August_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
